rem the server of the 395 runs at -c 262144 with its buffers for the full context, llama-bench does the same
if not defined BENCHCTX   set "BENCHCTX=262144"
goto :defaults_done

:cuda_defaults
rem ---- 3090 / cuda: the experts of the first layers on the cpu, -ncmoe depends on the card ----
if not defined EXTRA      set "EXTRA=-ngl 99 -ncmoe 30"
if not defined CHECKARMS  set "CHECKARMS=default"
rem 09.10: pool32 (QSA key pool in f32) mean KLD 0.01768 against 0.01783 of the f16 default (repeat 0.010); PP at 122880
rem 605.5 against 616.5, TG the same, moe-cache slots +1-2 with f16. the arm is off
if not defined QARMS      set "QARMS=default;nofusion GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_FUSION=1"
rem the server setup of models.ini: the VRAM cache of hot experts and the memory layout per phase
rem 10.10: -b 8192 -ub 8192 (n2ub8k): the 118K prompt at 607.0 t/s against 527.6 with 4096, --phase-mem took ubatch
rem 6656 at 106K cells and 5888 at 120K (the memory); TG 26.86 against 27.40, acceptance 0.512 against 0.523 (text)
rem 12.10 night (f4a7d3ee): -b 16384 (b16k) took the 118K prompt at 903.9 t/s against 875.1 with -b 8192: --phase-mem plans
rem the buffers at every llama_decode call of a prompt (0.15-0.25 s each, 15 calls of the 118K prompt at -b 8192, 8 at
rem 16384), and the PLE rows of the second ubatch of a call are gathered while the first computes (the log line is
rem there). the default since then; prompts up to 8192 tokens are one ubatch either way
if not defined DECARGS    set "DECARGS=-fit off -ncmoe 48 --moe-cache auto --phase-mem --no-repack -b 16384 -ub 8192"
rem since 05.10 the cpu experts run while the gpu runs the cached ones (06.10: TG +2 percent, +4.6 with MTP n2;
rem GGML_SCHED_PARALLEL_CPU=0 turns it off) and a prompt of up to 192 tokens takes the generation layout with the
rem moe-cache kept (06.10: an 82-token prompt 1.6 s instead of 2.7 s, no 0.73 s refill after it;
rem LLAMA_PHASE_SMALL_PROMPT=0 turns it off). auto compares --spec-auto with the fixed n-max 2
rem 07.10: a context checkpoint takes 30-39 ms here, a short prompt is compute (three 31-token ubatches)
rem 07.10, the memory switches of 05.10 against base: lfu 26.38 against 24.55 t/s, then as the default 26.69 against
rem 24.13 of lru, every request faster in both runs (n2 29.54 against 26.92); compact 24.17 and async 24.35, no
rem gain; kvhost 111 slots instead of 68, TG +3.6 percent on the short prompts, -5 percent on the 2541-token one
rem and PP -7 percent
rem 08.10: nolid (no lightning indexer) TG 26.75 against 27.20, the same moe-cache slots (67-69), bench and KLD the
rem same. n2qsa (LLAMA_MTP_QSA=1): at a 500000-character prefix TG 25.40 against 26.93 of n2, acceptance 0.509
rem against 0.543 (texts diverge; at the same acceptance 3-5 percent slower), at prefix 0 about 4 percent slower:
rem the dense MTP block stays the default. the arms are off
rem 09.10, prof (GGML_SCHED_PROF=128), a decode step of 34-37 ms after the first 128 steps of a request (49-52 ms
rem while the moe-cache fills): 194 splits (97 CUDA, 97 CPU, 48 CPU splits without inputs run next to the GPU); the CPU
rem waits for the GPU 15.6-16.5 ms (the same at every hit rate), runs its experts 9-15 ms (440 MiB of host experts
rem per step, 30-45 GB/s), copies 2.6-3.3 ms (both ways), queues the CUDA splits 2 ms; 3 ms outside the scheduler,
rem 1.7 of them the moe-cache update (upload submission, table). TG of prof 26.72 against 26.79 of base.
rem 10.10, prof with GGML_SCHED_PROF_GPU=1: device busy 21.0-22.5 ms per step (the CUDA compute calls, with their host
rem launch, up to 3 ms), the CPU waits 16 ms: about 5 GB of weights a step would take 6 ms at 936 GB/s, so the GPU part
rem is the many small kernels of 97 compute calls, not the bandwidth. the timing events cost 3 percent (25.97 against
rem 26.73 of base). the arm is off, the switch stays
rem 09.10, stats (LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_STATS=2048, 8192 steps): at the real 68-69 slots and 1 upload per layer per step the
rem pooled caches lose: PLRU 62.5, PLFU 67.1 against LFU 68.0 and LRU 68.1 percent (the moe-cache measured 68.3).
rem the pool catches up only at 4-8 uploads per layer per step, PLRU 69.2 at 350 MiB of uploads per step against
rem 36 MiB of LFU. one pool for all layers (as upstream's --moe-cache-mib) is not taken; the arm is off
rem 09.10, n2 at a 500000-character prefix (118K tokens) with the MTP catch-up for the output rows only: PP 525.8 t/s
rem against 514.6 on 08.10, TG 27.58 against 26.93
rem 10.10, n2kv16k (LLAMA_PHASE_KV_STEP=16384, ubatch 4096): PP 540.1 against 527.6 of n2, 6 plans of the 118K prompt
rem instead of 29; a plan takes 0.19 s at 21K cells to 0.51 s at 123K, nearly all of it free (0.06-0.12 s, with the wait
rem for the previous batch) and reserve (0.11-0.38 s, the buffer allocation), the queries 0.01 s. at ubatch 8192 a plan
rem takes 0.66 s (7 queries of the ubatch search). n2kv32k: LLAMA_PHASE_KV_STEP=32768 on top of the 8192 ubatch
rem 10.10: auto 27.73 against 30.44 on 09.10, the online gate kept drafts off (length 0 in 2455 of 4645 cycles, verify
rem fitted at 28.6 ms + 18.5 ms per token), below base on the os prompts; n2 28.90 against 28.91. auto varies run to run
rem here, n2 does not
rem optime (11.10): GGML_CUDA_OP_TIMING=50000, the GPU time of every op of the decode (about 500 steps of 97 compute
rem calls per report in the server log, cuda_op_timing lines): where the 21 ms of device time of a step go against the
rem 6-7 ms its weights take at 936 GB/s. the CUDA graphs are off in this arm, its TG is not comparable
rem 11.10 (3afe15be7): base 26.39, n2 28.93, auto 29.12; n2 at the prefix PP 607.8 (the 120K prompt), TG 27.36.
rem n2kv32k 617.6 and 27.06: 63 plans of the prompt instead of 135 (40.9 s against 72.5 in all), but a smaller ubatch
rem deep in the prompt (6912-7680); not the default, the arm is off.
rem optime: about 2800 ops per decode step (97 compute calls), so 7.5 us per op of the 21 ms of device time; the
rem timing events add 10-15 us to each op (61 ms per step in all). the largest: the hc injection matmul (f32, 1 row
rem of 10240 x 4 columns) 67 us x 96 per step: CUDA takes its f32 mat-vec on Ampere only up to 3 columns. it is 4 rows
rem of 1 column for 1-4 tokens now (swap0 = before). about 24 of the 58 ops of a layer are hc work (mix: norm, down,
rem scale, silu, up, pre, injection; combine: scale, sigmoid, scale, post), the next fusion candidates. the prompt:
rem TOP_K of the block selection 96 ms per call (12 per ubatch, 1.15 s of the 2.6K prompt): CCCL 3.4.3+ runs cub
rem DeviceTopK once per row; from 8 rows the radix select of top-k.cu now (GGML_CUDA_TOPK_RADIX=0 = upstream)
rem 11.10 evening (403e1429b): base 30.40 against 26.66 of swap0 (+14 percent, os/db/code/repeat 31.09 / 31.59 / 30.09
rem / 29.00); n2 29.31 (26.69 / 26.46 / 30.80 / 35.12), auto 28.88; n2 at the prefix PP 817.4 against 607.8 (the radix
rem top-k), TG 26.73. MTP pays only on code and repeated text now: the fit of auto puts a verified token at 19.4 ms
rem (its cpu experts) against a decode step of about 32 ms, and with the head on, prose runs 14-16 percent below base.
rem 12.10 (2e5, before the cap change; TG of the summary, then os / db / code / repeat): base 30.55, 31.4 / 31.7 /
rem 30.1 / 29.2; n2 29.22; auto (MTP + ngram-mod, cap 6) 28.21, 26.4 / 27.6 / 30.4 / 29.3; automtp (MTP, cap 6) 29.80,
rem 26.9 / 28.0 / 30.7 / 35.2; automtp3 (MTP, cap 3, the user's setup) 31.74, 29.5 / 30.4 / 31.1 / 37.1, the best: +4
rem percent over base, prose still 4-6 percent below it. ngram-mod costs 17 percent on the repeated text here (auto
rem against automtp; on the 395 it gave +16): auto fitted 34.2 ms fixed per verify against 26.0, and gated 63 percent
rem of the cycles to no draft against 56. verify per token: 13.7 ms at the cap 3, 19.0 at 6 (recurrent state 450
rem against 788 MiB). since 12.10 --spec-auto takes the cap 3 and adds no ngram-mod: auto is the user's setup now
rem (MTP at the cap 3, as automtp3). n2 and the cap 6 are off.
rem maskdense: see the 395; here the mask was n_kv x 8192 f16 on both sides (about 1.9 GB each at the 120K prompt),
rem so the expert cache should get more slots, and the prompt loses the fill and the PCIe copy of it per ubatch
rem 12.10 afternoon (9519cec3d): base 30.60, auto 31.94, maskdense 30.98; the 120K prompt: auto 868.4 t/s against 827.1
rem of maskdense (the mask no longer copied over PCIe), TG 29.57 / 29.50; expert cache 48-51 slots in both, the prompt
rem compute 2932 against 2562 MiB (the selection after the mask fill, see the 395). bench: default 971.3 / 822.1,
rem maskdense 1018.0 / 851.7 at 0 / 122880 (the slow REPEAT of the -inf, see the 395). maskdense is off here
rem t8p / t16p: the CPU experts on the P-cores of the i9-12900K only (logical CPUs 0-15 are the 8 P-cores with HT, 16-23
rem the E-cores): one thread per P-core / both threads of each; the default takes 16 threads wherever Windows puts them,
rem and the slowest expert thread decides a layer. Strata moved its non-pool threads off the pool cores: +10-11 percent
rem decode on a Linux Xeon
rem auto at the prefix: the long prompt after the mask order fix, the one-element REPEAT as a fill and the PLE rows
rem gathered ahead (868.4 t/s on 12.10 afternoon)
rem 12.10 evening (49f): base 30.28, auto 32.09 (the HC fusions of 12.10 within the noise), t8p 28.45, t16p 29.97: the
rem P-cores alone lose, the E-cores help the CPU experts, so the CPU part matters here. t20 / t24: more threads, no pin.
rem the 120K prompt 875.1 t/s (868.4 before), TG 28.11. b16k: see the 395 (-b 16384 with -ub 8192: two per call)
rem the run of 12.10 night is a short one: no 01/03 (CUDA kernels unchanged since the evening check), bench at 0 and
rem 122880 for the alloc peak lines of default and maskdense, decode: auto against t20/t24 and b16k at the 118K prompt
rem (auto there: 875.1 on 12.10 evening)
rem 12.10 night (f4a7d3ee): auto 31.56, t20 31.80, t24 29.54 t/s, but the mean hides the text: on the six os/db/code runs
rem auto 31.17, t20 30.12 (-3.4 percent), t24 29.35 (-5.8), t20 wins only on repeat, where the acceptance moves
rem everything. more threads do not help the CPU experts (the RAM, not the cores), the default stays; b16k: see DECARGS
rem the next run is the per-op profile only (see PROFARMS)
if not defined DECARMS    set "DECARMS=auto @draft --spec-auto @p=0"
if not defined RUN_DECODE  set "RUN_DECODE=0"
if not defined RUN_BENCH   set "RUN_BENCH=0"
if not defined RUN_CHECK   set "RUN_CHECK=0"
if not defined RUN_QUALITY set "RUN_QUALITY=0"
if not defined BENCHDEPTHS set "BENCHDEPTHS=0,122880"
if not defined BENCHSMALL  set "BENCHSMALL=0"
if not defined GGML_ALLOC_PEAK set "GGML_ALLOC_PEAK=1"
if not defined DECPREFIX  set "DECPREFIX=0 500000"
rem 09.10, pp8k / ub8k: a prompt of 8192 tokens in two ubatches of 4096 against one of 8192 (with the experts on the
rem cpu every ubatch uploads nearly all of them over PCIe, a larger ubatch halves that per token): PP 684.7 against
rem 757.0 at depth 0, 636.2 against 725.0 at 65536 (+14 percent). the arms are off; the server takes -b/-ub 8192 since 10.10
rem topkcub (11.10 evening, GGML_CUDA_TOPK_RADIX=0: the top-k of a prompt ubatch row by row with cub, as before): PP
rem 696.8 / 623.7 against 1016.5 / 854.0 with the radix select (+46 and +37 percent at 0 and 122880), TG the same;
rem 01 TOP_K 531/531. the arm is off
rem 12.10 night (f4a7d3ee): maskdense (the dense KQ mask instead of the one from positions) PP 1015.9 / 858.6 against
rem 969.2 / 828.6 of the default at 0 / 122880, +4.8 / +3.6 percent, about 190 ms per 4096 ubatch at both depths, so
rem not the size of the mask; TG the same. no alloc peak lines: llama-bench drops the log (they go to stderr since)
if not defined BENCHARMS  set "BENCHARMS=default;maskdense LLAMA_QSA_MASK_POS=0 @d=0,122880"
rem llama-bench has no expert cache: a profile of it says little about the server of the 3090. optime / optimemd:
rem GGML_CUDA_OP_TIMING with a period above the compute calls of the run, so the report comes once, when the context
rem goes: the GPU time of every op of the warmup and the two prompts of 4096 at depth 0, for the 190 ms that the mask
rem from positions costs (the table is of the whole run, three prompts, not of one ubatch)
if not defined RUN_PROFILE set "RUN_PROFILE=1"
if not defined PROFKINDS   set "PROFKINDS=pp@0"
if not defined PROFARMS    set "PROFARMS=optime GGML_CUDA_OP_TIMING=1000000000;optimemd GGML_CUDA_OP_TIMING=1000000000 LLAMA_QSA_MASK_POS=0"
if not defined KERNARMS   set "KERNARMS=default"
if not defined RUN_KERNELS set "RUN_KERNELS=0"
rem auto: -c of each depth is depth + prompt, as --phase-mem sizes the buffers in the server. at a fixed -c 262144
rem the buffers did not fit the 24 GB and the driver moved some to system memory: PP 115-145 or 285-430 t/s
rem from one process to the next on 05.10, the same within a process
if not defined BENCHCTX   set "BENCHCTX=auto"

:defaults_done
rem ---- the same on both ----
rem 01-check: test-backend-ops ops, "OP [regex of the case parameters]", separated by ;
if not defined CHECKOPS    set "CHECKOPS=MUL_MAT;MUL_MAT_ID;MUL_MAT_ID_FUSION;MUL_MAT_VEC_FUSION;MUL_MAT_RELU;MUL_MAT_HEADSUM;TOP_K;TOPK_QSA;LIGHTNING_INDEXER;LIGHTNING_INDEXER_UNIT;GET_ROWS;GATED_DELTA_NET;GATED_DELTA_NET_CACHE_FUSION;DSV4_HC_PRE;DSV4_HC_POST;HC_POST_GATE;SCALE_SILU;REPEAT;FLASH_ATTN_EXT n_kv_max=[1-9];RMS_NORM;RMS_NORM_SCALE;RMS_NORM_MUL_SIGMOID_MUL;SSM_CONV;CONCAT_SSM_CONV"
rem 02-bench: llama-bench, one run per arm and depth
if not defined BENCHDEPTHS set "BENCHDEPTHS=0,32768,65536,122880"
if not defined BENCHPP     set "BENCHPP=4096"
if not defined BENCHTG     set "BENCHTG=64"
if not defined BENCHUB     set "BENCHUB=4096"
if not defined BENCHREPS   set "BENCHREPS=3"
rem tokens of the warmup process of 02 and 05: llama-bench draws the same ones in every process, below 32768 with
rem msvc, and the warmup reads the PLE rows of those draws into the page cache (warm_page_cache in _run.py). auto: as
rem many as the deepest measured process draws (its depth, then every rep of its prompt and generation: 135360 at
rem 122880). 10.10: with 98304 the arm that went first to 122880 read the rest cold (452 against 212 ms of inputs)
rem and lost 5 percent PP: f16reg at 122880 in two runs
if not defined BENCHWARMTOKENS set "BENCHWARMTOKENS=auto"
rem 03-quality: llama-perplexity, KLD of each arm against QREF (empty: stable when built, else default).
rem a run holds the logits of half a chunk and the reference of a chunk in ram, 12 GB at 16384. at 32768
rem (24 GB) the 395 failed with bad allocation and row cache read errors on 05.10: the model takes the rest
if not defined QCTX        set "QCTX=16384"
if not defined QCHUNKS     set "QCHUNKS=2"
if not defined QUB         set "QUB=2048"
rem 04-decode: llama-server, one start per arm and DECPREFIX
if not defined DECCTX      set "DECCTX=262144"
if not defined DECPROMPTS  set "DECPROMPTS=os db code repeat"
if not defined DECSEEDS    set "DECSEEDS=1 2"
if not defined DECNGEN     set "DECNGEN=1024"
if not defined DECSAMP     set "DECSAMP=1.0 20 0.95"
if not defined DECPREFIX   set "DECPREFIX=0"
if not defined DECPORT     set "DECPORT=8097"
if not defined DECGREP     set "DECGREP=moe_cache:.*slots|moe_cache: policy|moe_cache_stats: +[0-9]+[*]|moe_cache_stats: .*fits|phase_mem:|sched_prof|buffer size|QSA KV in RAM|alloc peak|PLE rows of a ubatch"
rem 1: the warmup run of llama-bench, llama-perplexity and llama-server at start. 0 (--no-warmup): it only adds
rem load time and memory pressure, -lm dio reads the weights at load and the median of 02 drops a cold first rep
if not defined WARMUP      set "WARMUP=0"
rem 06-kernels: test-backend-ops perf of the model shapes at -ub 4096, "OP [regex of the case parameters]"
if not defined KERNOPS     set "KERNOPS=MUL_MAT_ID n_mats=512,n_used=10,b=0,m=[0-9]+,n=4096,;MUL_MAT_VEC_FUSION n_mats=512;MUL_MAT type_a=q8_0,type_b=f32,m=[0-9]+,n=4096,"
rem 05-profile: one ubatch of the prompt (pp) and one decode step (tg) at PROFDEPTH
if not defined PROFKINDS   set "PROFKINDS=pp"
if not defined PROFARMS    set "PROFARMS=default"
if not defined PROFDEPTH   set "PROFDEPTH=32768"
rem run-all.bat
if not defined RUN_BUILD   set "RUN_BUILD=1"
if not defined RUN_CHECK   set "RUN_CHECK=1"
if not defined RUN_BENCH   set "RUN_BENCH=1"
if not defined RUN_QUALITY set "RUN_QUALITY=1"
if not defined RUN_DECODE  set "RUN_DECODE=1"

rem multi-config generators (msvc) put the binaries in bin\Release, single-config in bin
set "BIN=%BUILD%\bin\Release"
if not exist "%BIN%" set "BIN=%BUILD%\bin"

set "LOGS=%~dp0logs"
if not exist "%LOGS%" mkdir "%LOGS%"

rem the scripts are a front for _run.py
set "PY="
where py >nul 2>&1
if not errorlevel 1 set "PY=py -3"
if defined PY goto :eof
where python >nul 2>&1
if not errorlevel 1 set "PY=python"
